If you're polymorphed and were levitating/flying and have water walking,
reverting by timing out does not cause you to fall into the water, but
polymorphing out explicitly does, e.g. #polyself.  Reverting happens via
rehumanize(), which doesn't do anything special with water.  On the other
hand, explicit polymorph goes through polyself()[1], with this block of code
at the end:

    if (is_pool(u.ux,u.uy) && was_floating && !(Levitation || Flying) &&
            !breathless(youmonst.data) && !amphibious(youmonst.data) &&
            !Swimming) drown();

This checks for levitation and flying after changing form, but not Wwalking
(water walking).  Easiest fix would be to add Wwalking to the condition,
though you have to wonder if this code is needed at all, given that
rehumanize() works fine without it.

[1]: http://nethackwiki.com/wiki/Polyself.c#polyself


